     "answer_markdown": "Backend Engineer is losing candidates mainly in the Technical Interview: 5 of 17 reached that stage moved on, 2 were rejected, and 5 withdrew, with 3 of those withdrawals blamed on waiting too long to be scheduled.\n\n| Stage | Reached | Moved on | Rejected | Withdrew | There now | Why people left |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Resume Review | 20 | 18 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1 rejected for missing a required skill |\n| Recruiter Screen | 18 | 17 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 rejected for interview feedback below the bar |\n| Technical Interview | 17 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 5 | 2 rejected for interview feedback below the bar; 3 withdrew for waited too long to be scheduled; 1 withdrew for personal reasons; 1 withdrew for accepted another offer |\n| Final Interview | 5 | 0 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 rejected for interview feedback below the bar; 1 withdrew for accepted another offer |\n\nThe biggest delay is in the Technical Interview scheduling clock: 14 of the 17 people who reached it are still past the 7-day booking target, and 3 people there now are still waiting to be booked, with waits of 12, 16, and 22 days. Final Interview also has a small slowdown, but it is a low sample.",
