     "answer_markdown": "Backend Engineer has been open 123 days, and the main losses are in the Technical Interview stage.\n\n| Stage | Reached | Moved on | Rejected | Withdrew | There now | Why people left |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Resume Review | 20 | 18 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1 rejected for a missing required skill |\n| Recruiter Screen | 18 | 17 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 rejected for interview feedback below the bar |\n| Technical Interview | 17 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 5 | 2 rejected for interview feedback below the bar; 3 withdrew because they waited too long to be scheduled; 1 withdrew for personal reasons; 1 withdrew after accepting another offer |\n\nTechnical Interview is the bottleneck: 14 of 17 people who reached it were still waiting to be scheduled past the 7-day booking target, and 3 of the 5 people there now are already past the 14-day time-in-stage target. Final Interview also has some friction, but the sample is small.\n\nNext steps:\n- Technical Interview: reduce scheduling delays; 14 of 17 reached it are past the booking target.\n- Technical Interview: review the 5 withdrawals, especially the 3 tied to waiting too long to be scheduled.\n- Final Interview: monitor the 2 people there now, since 1 is already past the time-in-stage target.",
